messages.text:
I am genuinely not collecting telemetry on this site beyond what Cloudflare collects, but Cloudflare’s is pretty detailed and could very probably allow me to take a reasonable guess at who sent an email, or at least rule in or out some people under some circumstances, so the honest answer is that you should probably use Tor (though you don’t need the awful clunky Tor browser - you can just install Tor with Homebrew, get it running with brew services, use a torrc slightly like mine below, stick the second file below wherever, go to settings -> privacy -> connections -> proxy in Firefox and add that file under automatic proxy configuration URL, and it will route requests to that website specifically over Tor and everything else normally)

ClientOnly 1
SocksPort 9050
UseEntryGuards 1
NumEntryGuards 1
CircuitBuildTimeout 10
LearnCircuitBuildTimeout 1
MaxCircuitDirtiness 1800
NewCircuitPeriod 600
ClientUseIPv6 0
MaxClientCircuitsPending 64
ExitNodes {gb},{nl},{de},{fr}
StrictNodes 0

function FindProxyForURL(url, host) {
    host = host.toLowerCase();
    if (shExpMatch(host, "sammail.cc")) return "SOCKS5 127.0.0.1:9050";
    else return "DIRECT";
}
